  "semantics": {
    "whole_child_cpu": "Linux wait4 resource usage includes the waited child thread group and resource usage of terminated descendants propagated through intervening waits. Excludes the supervising Python parent and other unrelated processes. No claim that an unobserved orphan/unwaited descendant was included.",
    "memory": "ru_maxrss is KiB on Linux. This is a per-process high-water/max across accounted descendants, not the simultaneous summed RSS of a process tree. Retains possible pre-exec image high-water; it is not Rust-only or pressure-phase-only RSS.",
    "timing": "CPU is user+system consumed time; wall_ns is the parent launch-to-reap observation including scheduler/polling delay. 1000ns storage resolution does not imply nanosecond measurement precision.",
    "nested_cost_rule": "Report exactly one chosen enclosing CPU scope, and use nested phase/actor/dispatch/Host counters only as breakdown diagnostics. Never add wait4 to phase totals, phase whole to its intervals, actor to containing process, or any of these to encompassing cgroup usage.",
    "rss_rule": "Do not sum RSS high-water values across phases, actors or processes to claim simultaneous peak; memory.current boundary snapshots also are not a peak.",
    "serialization": "Whole-child CPU covers final Rust report serialization and write system-call execution. It does not separately identify this CPU share or guarantee full physical storage flush cost. Parent hashing, JSON receipt writing and report acceptance occur after child exit and are not in this wait4 measurement.",
    "cgroup_rule": "cpu.stat usage_usec delta is a different, wider interval around the complete native driver, not confirmation-only CPU. Use the independently recorded usage counter; user/system microsecond rounding can differ by 1us. Throttled time is not CPU usage and must not be added.",
    "limits": "All eight before/after boundary snapshots exactly equal cpu.max=25000 100000, burst=0, memory.max=2147483648, memory.swap.max=0, pids.max=256. Same installed unit SHA and all eight actual-systemd before/after log bytes match. This is a 25ms CPU allowance per100ms period (0.25 CPU bandwidth), 2GiB memory, zero swap and256 kernel tasks/threads; not dedicated hardware."
  },
